{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the Svelte adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/svelte-form","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-form","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":" requires an options function and form-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":". Their\nshape becomes the form's inferred value type."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n      age: 0,\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"fullName\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Full name\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n        {#each field.errors as error}\n          <span role=\"alert\">{error.message}</span>\n        {/each}\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"age\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Age\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          type=\"number\"\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) =>\n            field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.valueAsNumber)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Subscribe\n    selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const}\n  >\n    {#snippet children([canSubmit, isSubmitting])}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n        {isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save'}\n      </button>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Subscribe>\n</form>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The important pieces are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" define the complete initial value and drive type inference."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Field"},{"type":"text","value":" subscribes to one field. Its child snippet exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.value"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta"},{"type":"text","value":", and event handlers."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validators are ordered objects with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" function and explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" updates only its child snippet when the selected form state\nchanges."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates the form before calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"create-a-form","text":"Create a form","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you.\n\nInstall the Svelte adapter:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-form\n```\n\n## Create a form\n\n`createForm` requires an options function and form-level `defaultValues`. Their\nshape becomes the form's inferred value type.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n      age: 0,\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"fullName\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Full name\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n        {#each field.errors as error}\n          <span role=\"alert\">{error.message}</span>\n        {/each}\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"age\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Age\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          type=\"number\"\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) =>\n            field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.valueAsNumber)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Subscribe\n    selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const}\n  >\n    {#snippet children([canSubmit, isSubmitting])}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n        {isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save'}\n      </button>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Subscribe>\n</form>\n```\n\nThe important pieces are:\n\n- `defaultValues` define the complete initial value and drive type inference.\n- `form.Field` subscribes to one field. Its child snippet exposes `field.value`,\n  `field.meta`, and event handlers.\n- Validators are ordered objects with a `run` function and explicit `triggers`.\n- `form.Subscribe` updates only its child snippet when the selected form state\n  changes.\n- `form.handleSubmit()` validates the form before calling `onSubmit`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nTanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you.\n\nInstall the Svelte adapter:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-form\n```\n\n## Create a form\n\n`createForm` requires an options function and form-level `defaultValues`. Their\nshape becomes the form's inferred value type.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n      age: 0,\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"fullName\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Full name\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) => field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.value)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n        {#each field.errors as error}\n          <span role=\"alert\">{error.message}</span>\n        {/each}\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Field\n    name=\"age\"\n    validators={[\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n    ]}\n  >\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <label>\n        Age\n        <input\n          name={field.name}\n          type=\"number\"\n          value={field.value}\n          onblur={field.handleBlur}\n          oninput={(event) =>\n            field.handleChange(event.currentTarget.valueAsNumber)}\n          aria-invalid={field.meta.isInvalid}\n        />\n      </label>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <form.Subscribe\n    selector={(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const}\n  >\n    {#snippet children([canSubmit, isSubmitting])}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n        {isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save'}\n      </button>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Subscribe>\n</form>\n```\n\nThe important pieces are:\n\n- `defaultValues` define the complete initial value and drive type inference.\n- `form.Field` subscribes to one field. Its child snippet exposes `field.value`,\n  `field.meta`, and event handlers.\n- Validators are ordered objects with a `run` function and explicit `triggers`.\n- `form.Subscribe` updates only its child snippet when the selected form state\n  changes.\n- `form.handleSubmit()` validates the form before calling `onSubmit`.\n"}
